Chapter: BvtPulseRoots
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter GameCombatDress
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 The composite pulse runs once per session, so a walk of every root object there costs sessions times the world
 (Damian, 2026-10-18: "we need to keep the quadratic situation of message to everyone bounded as much as possible to
 small regions"). Boot's cgl-arrange removes the combat fixtures, so the monster stage has none to dress.
  bpo-map : WalkMap = WalkMap { x = 0, y = 0, width = 0, height = 0, land = 0, solids = 0, stride = 0, refused = 0 }
  bpo-fixture : CompositeGame -> Integer
  bpo-fixture (owner) = let game = owner.checkpoint.game
    in when world-create game.world (gs-mobile 0 1430 1700 0 400 1002)
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (serial) -> if cb-profile owner.combat game serial "Sparring partner" 10 1 1 0 /= 0 then 0 else serial
  bvt-pulse-roots : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-pulse-roots (unused) = when cg-new 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("pulse roots fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> let game = owner.checkpoint.game
      in let skipped = bpo-fixture owner
      in let staged = cg-monsters-base owner game (gn-input 1) bpo-map 0 0
      in let bare = skipped /= 0 & gmb-layer owner.items skipped 11 0 == 0
      in let kept = bpo-fixture owner
      in let dressed = cbd-dress owner.combat owner.items 0
      in let styled = kept /= 0 & gmb-layer owner.items kept 11 0 > 0
      in act
        a <- bvt-check "the composite monster stage walks no root object: a combat fixture stays undressed" (is-ok staged & bare)
        b <- bvt-check "the standalone combat server's dress still styles a fixture" (is-ok dressed & styled)
        a + b
      end
